<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mathurin-Léonard Duphot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1769">1769</a>–<a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mathurin-Léonard Duphot was a French general of the Revolutionary Wars who served under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. In December 1797 he was shot by papal troops during a riot outside the French embassy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. His death gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-directory">French Directory</a> a pretext to occupy Rome under General Berthier and proclaim the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> in February 1798.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mathurin-leonard-duphot.jpg" alt="Mathurin-Léonard Duphot" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: H. Rousseau (graphic designer), E. Mons (engraver) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AduC_238_Duphot_(L.,_1769-1797).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
